{:kotoba.stdlib/version 3
 :kotoba.stdlib/release "0.3.0"
 :kotoba.stdlib/public-names-manifest "lang/conformance/stdlib/manifest.edn"
 :kotoba.stdlib/wbs "T4.1"
 :kotoba.stdlib/artifacts
 [{:id :core
   :path "stdlib/core.kotoba"
   :namespace stdlib.core
   :sha256 "777b60898f5052e6346b4f0710ed90f0cec5517dff5ebfb464abb3cbd6fe0c30"}]
 ;; Version 3 (2026-09-02) added eleven clojure.core names; what was asked for
 ;; and refused is recorded, message by message, in the manifest's :absent.
 :kotoba.stdlib/absent "lang/conformance/stdlib/manifest.edn :absent"
 ;; WHAT ADMITS PORTABLE LIBRARY SOURCE. The invariant has not changed --
 ;; library source is compiled WITH the program and never loaded from ambient
 ;; runtime state -- but this key once named a route that does not carry it,
 ;; and a route that fails closed reads exactly like one that worked.
 :kotoba.stdlib/import-policy
 {:mode :explicit-source-path
  :cli ["compile" "--source-path"]
  :ambient-default false
  :reason "Portable library source is admitted and compiled with the program; it is never loaded from ambient runtime state. The project route resolves a CLOSED module graph from explicit source roots -- namespace to path, one file per namespace, symlink escape and cross-root ambiguity refused -- which is a stronger form of the same invariant than prepending a file: nothing enters the build that a (:require ...) in the graph did not name."
  :example "amu check <entry> --source-path <app dir> --source-path <lib dir> --jvm-free"
  :jvm-free true

  ;; `--prelude` is not a route. Measured 2026-09-01 against amu 93c4998:
  :superseded-cli
  {:flag "--prelude"
   :status :not-implemented-anywhere
   :measured
   {:as-of "2026-09-01"
    :amu "93c4998"
    :nbb-route "amu check app.kotoba --prelude lang/stdlib/core.kotoba --jvm-free exits 64: '--prelude is not implemented on this route and would be silently ignored; only the CLJS backend reads it.'"
    :jvm-route "silently ignored. kotoba.compiler.cli reads flags by name (option/options); an unrecognised one is skipped without comment, and the string \"prelude\" does not occur in that file."
    :cljs-backend "does NOT read it either, contrary to what the launcher's own refusal message says. kotoba.compiler.backend.cljs/emit takes [kir fuel]; its `prelude-forms` is the emitted fuel/quot RUNTIME prelude, not a source file. The string \"--prelude\" occurs nowhere in amu outside bin/amu's refusal and the launcher test that pins it."
    :correction "the launcher refuses for a good reason and the refusal should stand; only its stated scope is too generous. Reported, not changed here -- bin/amu belongs to kotoba-lang/amu."}}

  ;; The artifact is now reachable through the route named above. What follows
  ;; is the measurement, not a claim: commands, exit codes, and the value the
  ;; emitted artifact returns.
  :artifact-reachability
  {:status :reachable
   :as-of "2026-09-01"
   :amu "27d82d8"
   :kotoba-lang "df17122"
   :evidence
   [{:what "the package SSoT is the source root"
     :command "amu check lang/conformance/stdlib/basic.kotoba --source-path lang --jvm-free"
     :exit 0
     :result "{:ok true ... :project {:root stdlib.basic, :module-order [stdlib.core stdlib.basic], :paths {stdlib.core <repo>/lang/stdlib/core.kotoba ...}}}"}
    {:what "the conformance mirror is the source root"
     :command "amu check lang/conformance/stdlib/basic.kotoba --source-path lang/conformance --jvm-free"
     :exit 0
     :result "same, with stdlib.core resolved to lang/conformance/stdlib/core.kotoba"}
    {:what "it emits, and the artifact computes the conformance case's expected value"
     :command "amu compile lang/conformance/stdlib/basic.kotoba --source-path lang --unpinned --target wasm32 --output basic.wasm --jvm-free"
     :exit 0
     :result "3413-byte wasm32-kotoba-v1 artifact; instantiated through amu runtime/browser-host.mjs, main() = 9n, which is the case's :expect {:kotoba 9}"}
    {:what "the version-3 names emit and compute (2026-09-02, amu bb51dc14)"
     :command "amu compile lang/conformance/stdlib/extended.kotoba --source-path lang --unpinned --target wasm32 --output extended.wasm --jvm-free"
     :exit 0
     :result "5355-byte wasm32-kotoba-v1 artifact; instantiated through amu runtime/browser-host.mjs, main() = 678392943530n, one term per new name on its own power of ten (the case's :expect)"}]
   :jvm-free-note "bin/amu routes project mode to the nbb path (amu#717, merge bf1ae6c). The three commands above ran with --jvm-free, which refuses the Clojure/JVM compatibility path rather than falling back to it."

   ;; What it took to get here, because two of the four were language-level and
   ;; are the reason the frozen public-names list moved.
   :blockers-cleared
   [{:id :no-namespace-form
     :was "the file declared no (ns ...) and no (:export ...). Requiring stdlib.core with --source-path was refused: 'project module requires exactly one namespace'."
     :fixed-by "(ns stdlib.core (:export [...])). The file did not move: namespace-to-path is dots-to-slashes with hyphens to underscores, so stdlib.core resolves to <root>/stdlib/core.kotoba under either lang or lang/conformance."
     :diagnostic-defect "the refusal names the ENTRY module as :source, not the module that lacks the namespace, which reads as though the caller's own file is at fault. Not fixed here -- the diagnostic belongs to kotoba-lang/amu."}
    {:id :empty-defrecord
     :was "(defrecord None []) is refused with :kotoba.error/record-fields, 'record fields must be a non-empty unique bounded vector'. Isolated: a two-line file containing only (defrecord None []) and a main is refused the same way, and the same file with (defrecord Some [value]) is admitted."
     :decision :refusal-stands
     :fixed-by "the records were withdrawn, not respelled. See lang/conformance/stdlib/manifest.edn :records and the workspace ADR below."}
    {:id :reserved-names
     :was "five of the twenty-seven frozen public names are RESERVED: option-some, option-none, option-some?, option-value (the language owns Option/Result) and some (a reserved head, in the same set as let, if and ns). 'reserved function name'."
     :fixed-by "withdrawn; some was renamed first-match."
     :note "this blocker was NOT in the previous record of this key. It only becomes visible after the first two are cleared, which is why re-measuring found more than had been written down."}
    {:id :eleven-functions-no-longer-admitted
     :was "with the records and the reserved names out of the way, eleven of the file's functions still did not admit as written: option-some?, option-none?, option-value, ok?, err?, unwrap-ok, unwrap-err, find, select-keys, update, group-by."
     :fixed-by "withdrawn, with the refusing message recorded name by name."}]

   ;; Two limits are the reason the surviving list is smaller than it could be.
   ;; Both are outside this repository.
   :limits-encountered
   [{:id :multi-arity-export
     :owner "kotoba-lang/amu"
     :message "export does not name a declared function"
     :detail "a module is analyzed before it is linked, so (defn twice ([x] ...) ([x y] ...)) is already twice$arity$1 and twice$arity$2 when (:export [twice]) is resolved. range therefore takes three arguments here rather than one, two or three."}
    {:id :wasm32-typed-values
     :owner "kotoba-lang/amu"
     :detail "an if whose arms are (option-some x) and (option-none) is 'unsupported typed Wasm expression'; map-new / map-assoc is an internal compiler error. find and update admit and run on the KIR backend and are withdrawn only because this package claims :kotoba-wasm."}]}

  ;; The same claim was carried elsewhere. Three of the four are corrected now.
  :also-claimed-in
  [{:path "lang/cli.edn"
    :at ":compile options, :id :prelude"
    :says "Explicit portable source prelude prepended before the entry source."
    :status "STILL UNCORRECTED. Specified by this authority, refused by the implementation. Removing a documented CLI option is a language decision with its own conformance surface (scripts/check-cli-contract.bb, lang/cli-adapter-matrix.edn), not a side effect of making the stdlib reachable."}
   {:path "lang/surface-status.edn"
    :at ":portable-source-stdlib"
    :status "corrected 2026-09-01: :import-policy :explicit-prelude -> :explicit-source-path, the :cli-conformance command, the release, and :includes, which named Option and Result the package no longer carries. Was STALE AGAIN for part of 2026-09-02 (:release said 0.2.0 while this package was 0.3.0, manifest version 3; not corrected in the same change because that file was under concurrent edit). Corrected later the same day: :release 0.3.0, :measured :as-of 2026-09-02 with the extended-case evidence."}
   {:path "lang/conformance/manifest.edn"
    :at "case :portable-source-stdlib"
    :status "corrected 2026-09-01: the unread :prelude key is replaced by :source-paths, which is what the case actually is."}
   {:path "docs/lang/option-result-guide.md"
    :at "the two-layer table and section 3"
    :status "corrected 2026-09-01: the stdlib prelude layer is gone; section 3 now documents the language builtins that took those names."}]}
